(37, 'Argil Tiles at MosBuild 2026 Moscow: Quartz & SPC Flooring Showcase', 'argil-tiles-at-mosbuild-2026-moscow-quartz-spc-flooring-showcase', '<p>Argil Tiles is delighted to announce its participation in&nbsp;<strong>MosBuild 2026</strong>, one of the most prominent international exhibitions for building materials and interior solutions. The event will be held at&nbsp;<strong>Crocus Expo</strong> in&nbsp;<strong>Moscow</strong> from&nbsp;<strong>31st March to 3rd April 2026</strong>.</p><p>As a rapidly growing global brand, Argil Tiles continues to expand its presence in international markets by showcasing innovative, high-quality surface solutions tailored for modern architecture and interior design.</p><h4><strong>About MosBuild 2026</strong></h4><p>MosBuild is Russia’s leading international exhibition dedicated to construction, building materials, and interior design industries. The event attracts thousands of professionals including architects, designers, developers, manufacturers, and distributors from across the globe.</p><p>It serves as a powerful platform for:</p><ul><li>Exploring new products and technologies</li><li>Understanding global market trends</li><li>Connecting with industry leaders</li><li>Expanding business opportunities across regions</li></ul><h4><strong>Argil Tiles at MosBuild 2026</strong></h4><p>Argil Tiles will be presenting its premium product range, offering visitors an opportunity to explore quality, innovation, and design excellence.</p><p><strong>Exhibition Details:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Event:</strong> MosBuild 2026</li><li><strong>Venue:</strong> Crocus Expo, Moscow</li><li><strong>Dates:</strong> 31 March – 3 April 2026</li><li><strong>Pavilion:</strong> 2</li><li><strong>Hall:</strong> 8</li><li><strong>Stand No.:</strong> H7039</li></ul><h4><strong>Showcasing Innovation: Our Key Product Lines</strong></h4><p>Argil Tiles will be highlighting its advanced product categories that meet international quality standards and evolving design requirements.</p><h4><strong>Dura Quartz – Unique &amp; Versatile Surfaces</strong></h4><p>Dura Quartz surfaces are engineered to deliver a perfect blend of durability and aesthetics. These surfaces are ideal for both residential and commercial applications, offering long-lasting performance with elegant finishes.</p><p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p><ul><li>High resistance to scratches and stains</li><li>Easy maintenance and cleaning</li><li>Wide range of colors and textures</li><li>Suitable for countertops, walls, and interior applications</li></ul><h4><strong>LinkLock SPC Flooring – The Future of Flooring</strong></h4><p>LinkLock SPC flooring is a modern flooring solution designed for durability, performance, and ease of installation. It is widely used in both residential and commercial environments.</p><p><strong>Key Advantages:</strong></p><ul><li>100% water-resistant</li><li>Strong and stable core structure</li><li>Easy click-lock installation system</li><li>Termite and fire resistant</li><li>Suitable for high-traffic areas</li></ul><h4><strong>Strengthening Global Presence</strong></h4><p>Participation in&nbsp;<strong>MosBuild 2026</strong> reflects Argil Tiles’ commitment to expanding its reach in international markets, particularly in Russia and Europe.</p><p>This exhibition provides an opportunity to engage directly with global buyers, understand market demands, and establish long-term business relationships. It also enables Argil Tiles to showcase its capabilities as a reliable exporter of premium surface solutions.</p><h4><strong>Visit Us in Moscow</strong></h4><p>We invite industry professionals to visit our stand and explore our latest product innovations.</p><p><strong>Stand Details:</strong><br>Pavilion 2 | Hall 8 | Stand H7039</p><p>📩&nbsp;<strong>Email:</strong> info@argiltiles.com<br>🌐&nbsp;<strong>Website:</strong> www.argiltiles.com</p><h4><strong>Conclusion</strong></h4><p>MosBuild 2026 represents a significant milestone for Argil Tiles as it continues to grow its global footprint. With a focus on quality, innovation, and customer satisfaction, Argil Tiles is ready to present its advanced quartz and SPC flooring solutions to the international market.</p><p>Join us in&nbsp;<strong>Moscow</strong> and explore the future of surfaces with Argil Tiles.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', '1783680102_blog4.jpg', 'active', '2026-03-26 12:22:49', '2026-07-10 05:11:42'),
(38, 'Best Flooring for Different Climates: What Works in Heat, Humidity & Cold?', 'best-flooring-for-different-climates-what-works-in-heat-humidity-cold', '<p>Flooring plays a foundational role in any space, influencing not only aesthetics but also comfort, durability, and long-term maintenance. While design and cost are often the primary considerations, climate is an equally important factor that is frequently overlooked.</p><p>Different regions experience varying environmental conditions such as extreme heat, high humidity, or cold temperatures. These factors directly impact how flooring materials behave over time. A surface that performs exceptionally well in one climate may deteriorate quickly in another.</p><p>This guide provides a detailed understanding of how to select flooring based on climatic conditions, ensuring both performance and longevity.</p><h4><strong>Understanding the Impact of Climate on Flooring</strong></h4><p>Every flooring material reacts differently to environmental exposure:</p><ul><li><strong>Heat</strong> can cause expansion and fading</li><li><strong>Moisture</strong> can lead to swelling, mold, or structural weakening</li><li><strong>Cold temperatures</strong> can make surfaces brittle or uncomfortable</li></ul><p>Ignoring these factors often results in premature wear, higher maintenance costs, and reduced lifespan of the flooring.</p><h4><strong>Flooring Solutions for Hot Climates</strong></h4><p>Regions with consistently high temperatures require flooring that remains stable and does not absorb excessive heat.</p><h4><strong>Recommended Materials</strong></h4><p><strong>1. Vitrified Tiles</strong><br>Vitrified tiles are one of the most reliable options for hot climates. Their low porosity and high durability make them resistant to heat and surface damage. They also retain a relatively cool surface, which enhances indoor comfort.</p><p><strong>2. Ceramic Tiles</strong><br>Ceramic tiles are widely preferred due to their affordability and ease of maintenance. They do not warp under heat and are available in a wide range of finishes suitable for modern interiors.</p><p><strong>3. Natural Stone (Marble, Granite)</strong><br>Natural stones offer excellent thermal resistance and remain naturally cool. They are particularly suitable for premium residential and commercial spaces.</p><h4><strong>Design Considerations</strong></h4><ul><li>Opt for&nbsp;<strong>lighter shades</strong> to reflect heat</li><li>Use&nbsp;<strong>larger tiles</strong> to reduce grout lines and heat absorption</li><li>Ensure proper installation to avoid cracks due to expansion</li></ul><h4><strong>Flooring for Humid and Coastal Regions</strong></h4><p>Moisture is the biggest challenge in humid climates. Flooring must be resistant to water absorption and should not support mold or fungal growth.</p><h4><strong>Recommended Materials</strong></h4><p><strong>1. SPC Flooring (Stone Plastic Composite)</strong><br>SPC flooring has emerged as a highly effective solution for moisture-prone areas. Its rigid core structure and waterproof properties make it ideal for kitchens, basements, and coastal regions.</p><p><strong>2. Porcelain Tiles</strong><br>Porcelain tiles are dense and have very low water absorption rates. They are durable, easy to maintain, and suitable for both residential and commercial applications.</p><p><strong>3. Quartz Surfaces</strong><br>Quartz is non-porous and highly resistant to moisture. It is particularly effective for areas like kitchens and bathrooms where hygiene and durability are critical.</p><h4><strong>Materials to Avoid</strong></h4><ul><li>Solid wood flooring</li><li>Low-quality laminates</li><li>Porous stones without proper sealing</li></ul><h3><strong>Practical Tips</strong></h3><ul><li>Ensure proper ventilation</li><li>Use anti-skid finishes in wet areas</li><li>Focus on materials with&nbsp;<strong>low maintenance requirements</strong></li></ul><h4><strong>Flooring for Cold Climates</strong></h4><p>Cold environments demand flooring that can provide comfort while maintaining structural integrity under temperature variations.</p><h4><strong>Recommended Materials</strong></h4><p><strong>1. Engineered Wood Flooring</strong><br>Engineered wood offers better dimensional stability compared to solid wood. It adapts well to temperature changes while providing a warm and comfortable surface.</p><p><strong>2. SPC Flooring</strong><br>SPC flooring performs consistently across temperature fluctuations. It does not expand or contract significantly, making it suitable for colder regions.</p><p><strong>3. Carpet (Selective Use)</strong><br>Carpet can be used in specific areas like bedrooms to enhance warmth and comfort, although it requires higher maintenance.</p><h4><strong>Design Considerations</strong></h4><ul><li>Incorporate&nbsp;<strong>insulation layers</strong> beneath flooring</li><li>Choose materials that retain warmth</li><li>Avoid overly hard and cold surfaces in living areas</li></ul><h4><strong>Key Decision Factors</strong></h4><p>When selecting flooring based on climate, consider the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Durability under environmental stress</strong></li><li><strong>Resistance to water and temperature changes</strong></li><li><strong>Ease of maintenance</strong></li><li><strong>Long-term cost efficiency</strong></li></ul><p>A well-informed decision not only enhances performance but also reduces future repair and replacement costs.</p><h4><strong>Expert Perspective</strong></h4><p>Modern design practices increasingly favor a&nbsp;<strong>combination of materials</strong> rather than relying on a single solution. For example:</p><ul><li>Using&nbsp;<strong>SPC flooring in moisture-prone areas</strong></li><li>Incorporating&nbsp;<strong>tiles or stone in high-temperature zones</strong></li></ul><p>This approach ensures optimal performance across different parts of a property.</p><h4><strong>Conclusion</strong></h4><p>Climate-responsive flooring is essential for achieving durability, comfort, and long-term value. By selecting materials that align with environmental conditions, property owners can significantly enhance the lifespan and functionality of their spaces.</p><p>Investing in the right flooring today ensures fewer complications and better performance in the years ahead.</p>', '1783680069_blog3.jpg', 'active', '2026-04-03 09:47:24', '2026-07-10 05:11:09'),
(42, 'How Flooring Colors & Textures Influence the Perception of Space', 'how-flooring-colors-textures-influence-the-perception-of-space', '<p>Flooring is one of the most influential design elements in any interior environment. Beyond its functional role, it significantly impacts how a space is perceived in terms of size, brightness, warmth, and overall ambiance.</p><p>The choice of color, texture, and finish can subtly alter the psychological experience of a space. Understanding these effects allows homeowners, designers, and architects to create environments that are not only visually appealing but also emotionally comfortable.</p><h3><strong>The Role of Color in Spatial Perception</strong></h3><p>Color is a powerful visual tool that can change how a room is experienced.</p><h4><strong>Light-Colored Flooring</strong></h4><p>Light shades such as white, beige, and soft grey are widely used to create a sense of openness. They reflect natural and artificial light, making spaces appear larger and more inviting.</p><p>These colors are particularly effective in:</p><ul><li>Compact apartments</li><li>Offices with limited natural light</li><li>Minimalist interior designs</li></ul><h4><strong>Dark-Colored Flooring</strong></h4><p>Dark tones such as deep brown, charcoal, and black introduce depth and sophistication. They create a strong visual contrast and are often associated with luxury interiors.</p><p>However, they are best suited for:</p><ul><li>Larger spaces</li><li>Well-lit areas</li><li>Feature zones</li></ul><h4><strong>Neutral and Natural Tones</strong></h4><p>Wood-inspired and earthy shades strike a balance between light and dark tones. They offer versatility and blend seamlessly with various design styles.</p><p>These tones are ideal for:</p><ul><li>Living rooms</li><li>Bedrooms</li><li><p>Contemporary and traditional interiors</p><p>&nbsp;</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Importance of Texture and Finish</strong></h3><p>The surface finish of flooring plays a critical role in both aesthetics and functionality.</p><h4><strong>Glossy Finish</strong></h4><p>Glossy surfaces reflect light effectively, enhancing brightness and creating a polished appearance. They are suitable for modern interiors but require regular maintenance to keep them clean.</p><h4><strong>Matte Finish</strong></h4><p>Matte finishes offer a subtle and refined look. They are less prone to visible dust and scratches, making them practical for high-traffic areas.</p><h4><strong>Textured Surfaces</strong></h4><p>Textured flooring adds depth and character while also improving grip and safety. It is particularly useful in areas exposed to moisture or heavy use.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4><strong>Impact on Space Perception</strong></h4><p>Flooring choices can visually alter the dimensions of a room:</p><ul><li><strong>Large-format tiles</strong> create a seamless and expansive look</li><li><strong>Continuous flooring across rooms</strong> enhances spatial flow</li><li><strong>Patterns and contrasts</strong> can define specific zones</li></ul><p>Careful selection ensures that the flooring complements the overall layout and purpose of the space.</p><h4><strong>Psychological Influence</strong></h4><p>Different flooring choices evoke different emotional responses:</p><ul><li>Light tones create a sense of calm and clarity</li><li>Dark tones evoke warmth and sophistication</li><li>Natural textures promote comfort and relaxation</li></ul><p>These subtle effects contribute to how people experience and interact with a space.</p><h4><strong>Practical Application</strong></h4><p>To achieve the best results:</p><ul><li>Use lighter tones in smaller areas</li><li>Incorporate darker shades in feature spaces</li><li>Choose finishes based on usage and maintenance needs</li><li>Balance visual appeal with long-term practicality</li></ul><h4><strong>Conclusion</strong></h4><p>Flooring is not merely a design element; it is a strategic decision that influences both aesthetics and user experience. By understanding the relationship between color, texture, and perception, it is possible to create interiors that are functional, comfortable, and visually harmonious.</p><p>A thoughtful approach to flooring selection ensures that spaces not only look good but also feel right.</p>', '1783680027_blog2.jpg', 'active', '2026-04-20 10:20:11', '2026-07-10 05:10:27'),
(45, 'Argil Tiles India to UK Export Story: Premium Quartz & SPC Flooring Supply', 'argil-tiles-india-to-uk-export-story-premium-quartz-spc-flooring-supply', '<p>The UK construction and interior design market is evolving rapidly, with increasing demand for modern, durable, and cost-efficient flooring solutions. As projects expand across residential, commercial, and hospitality sectors, import reliance continues to grow.</p><p>Argil Tiles, based in India, is actively contributing to this demand by supplying premium Quartz surfaces and SPC flooring solutions designed specifically for international standards, including the UK market. The focus remains on quality consistency, design alignment, and reliable export supply.</p><h4><strong>Growing Flooring Demand in the UK Construction Market</strong></h4><p>The UK construction sector continues to show steady growth, supported by ongoing housing developments, urban redevelopment projects, and infrastructure modernization. Residential construction remains a major driver, while commercial spaces such as offices, retail outlets, and hospitality environments are also undergoing continuous upgrades.</p><p>This growth has directly increased the demand for flooring materials that are not only visually appealing but also capable of handling long-term usage. Import-based sourcing has become a practical solution for many UK developers due to cost efficiency and product availability.</p><h4><strong>Design Expectations in Modern UK Interiors</strong></h4><p>Interior design trends in the UK have shifted significantly toward clean, minimal, and functional aesthetics. There is a strong preference for flooring that blends natural stone-inspired looks with modern engineering performance.</p><p>At the same time, practicality remains equally important. Flooring materials are expected to offer resistance to moisture, scratches, and daily wear while maintaining their appearance over time. Easy installation and low maintenance requirements are also key factors influencing purchasing decisions.</p><p>As a result, materials like Quartz surfaces and SPC flooring are increasingly being chosen for both residential and commercial applications across the UK.</p><h4><strong>Quartz Surfaces for Premium Interior Applications</strong></h4><p>Quartz surfaces have become a preferred material in high-end interior design due to their balance of durability and visual appeal. In the UK market, Quartz is widely used in kitchens, bathrooms, hotel interiors, and commercial reception areas.</p><p>Its popularity is driven by its resistance to scratches and stains, along with its consistent surface finish that replicates natural stone while offering improved performance. Quartz also requires minimal maintenance, making it suitable for both luxury and high-usage environments.</p><p>Argil Tiles supplies export-grade Quartz surfaces that are manufactured to meet international quality expectations, ensuring consistency and reliability for large-scale projects.</p><h4><strong>SPC Flooring for Modern and Functional Spaces</strong></h4><p>SPC flooring has emerged as one of the fastest-growing flooring categories in the UK due to its strong performance characteristics. It is widely used in residential apartments, rental properties, offices, and retail environments.</p><p>The material is fully waterproof and highly resistant to impact, making it suitable for areas with heavy foot traffic or exposure to moisture. Its click-lock installation system simplifies the installation process, reducing labor time and cost.</p><p>SPC flooring also supports compatibility with underfloor heating systems, which is an important requirement in many UK homes and commercial buildings.</p><h4><strong>Why the UK Market Relies on Indian Tile Exporters</strong></h4><p>Indian manufacturers have become an important part of the global flooring supply chain due to their ability to deliver quality products at competitive pricing. The UK market, in particular, benefits from this balance of affordability and performance.</p><p>Exporters like Argil Tiles are able to offer scalability in production, which is essential for large construction projects. At the same time, customization options in design, texture, and finish allow UK buyers to align materials with specific architectural requirements.</p><p>Consistency in production and supply reliability further strengthens long-term partnerships between Indian exporters and UK importers.</p><h4><strong>Export Standards and Quality Control</strong></h4><p>To serve international markets effectively, strict quality control processes are followed throughout production and packaging. Every batch undergoes multiple checks to ensure dimensional accuracy, surface durability, and structural strength.</p><p>Packaging is designed to withstand long-distance shipping, reducing the risk of damage during transit. Moisture protection and reinforced handling standards are applied to ensure that products arrive in optimal condition.</p><p>These measures help maintain trust and reliability in export relationships, particularly in high-standard markets such as the UK.</p><h4><strong>Opportunities in the UK Flooring Industry</strong></h4><p>The UK flooring market continues to move toward materials that offer long-term value, sustainability, and design flexibility. There is growing demand for solutions that combine aesthetic appeal with functional performance.</p><p>Quartz and SPC flooring are positioned strongly within this trend due to their durability, modern appearance, and adaptability across different project types. As a result, import opportunities from India are expected to continue growing in the coming years.</p><h4><strong>Conclusion</strong></h4><p>The connection between India and the UK in the flooring industry is strengthening through consistent demand and reliable supply chains. Argil Tiles is positioned within this ecosystem by offering premium Quartz and SPC flooring solutions tailored for international requirements.</p><p>With a focus on quality, scalability, and export readiness, the company supports UK builders, importers, and developers seeking dependable flooring materials for modern construction needs.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', '1783679990_blog1.jpg', 'active', '2026-05-09 10:52:48', '2026-07-10 05:09:50');
INSERT INTO `case_studies` (`id`, `title`, `slug`, `short_description`, `overview`, `client_name`, `industry`, `location`, `project_type`, `project_area`, `challenge`, `solution`, `result`, `products_used`, `completion_date`, `featured_image`, `gallery`, `seo_title`, `seo_description`, `seo_keywords`, `status`, `is_featured`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(12, 'Premium Quartz Kitchen for a Modern Luxury Villa', 'premium-quartz-kitchen-for-a-modern-luxury-villa', 'Argil supplied premium engineered quartz slabs for a luxury residential kitchen, delivering elegant aesthetics, exceptional durability, and low-maintenance performance.', '<p>A newly constructed luxury villa required premium kitchen surfaces that combined timeless aesthetics with excellent durability. The homeowners wanted a marble-inspired appearance without the maintenance associated with natural stone. Argil\'s engineered quartz surfaces were selected for the kitchen countertops and island, offering superior stain resistance, scratch resistance, and long-lasting beauty suitable for everyday family living.</p>', 'Private Residential Project', 'Residential Construction', 'Ahmedabad, Gujarat', 'Quartz Surface', 'Kitchen Countertops & Island', '<p>The client wanted a luxurious stone appearance while avoiding the regular sealing and maintenance required by natural marble. The surface also needed to withstand daily cooking activities, spills, moisture, and frequent cleaning without losing its finish.</p>', '<p>Argil recommended premium engineered quartz slabs with a polished marble-inspired design. The slabs provided a non-porous surface, consistent color, and exceptional durability, making them ideal for modern residential kitchens.</p>', '<p>The completed kitchen achieved a sophisticated appearance with a bright and spacious feel. The quartz surfaces continue to provide easy maintenance, stain resistance, and lasting elegance while supporting the family\'s daily cooking requirements.</p>', 'Calacatta Inspired Quartz Slab, Polished Finish', '2025-12-03', '1783415457_gD4ABtBa.jpg', '\"[\\\"1783415457_3tuMhYaH.png\\\",\\\"1783415457_tYw0A3hj.png\\\",\\\"1783415457_9sT3cN0X.png\\\",\\\"1783415457_SSCMAjXm.png\\\"]\"', 'Luxury Villa Kitchen Quartz Surface Project | Argil', 'Discover how Argil engineered quartz transformed a luxury villa kitchen with elegant, durable, and low-maintenance surfaces.', 'quartz kitchen project,luxury villa quartz,engineered quartz kitchen,calacatta quartz', 'published', 1, '2026-07-07 01:29:53', '2026-07-07 03:40:57'),
(13, 'SPC Flooring Installation for a Corporate Office', 'spc-flooring-installation-for-a-corporate-office', 'Argil supplied durable SPC flooring for a modern office, combining fast installation with premium wood aesthetics.', '<p>A corporate office renovation required flooring that could be installed quickly while maintaining a professional appearance. The client wanted flooring capable of handling continuous employee movement with minimal maintenance. Argil SPC flooring was selected for its durability, dimensional stability, and realistic wood texture.</p>', 'Corporate Workspace Project', 'Commercial Office', 'Bengaluru, Karnataka', 'SPC Flooring', 'Office Workspace', '<p>The renovation schedule was limited, requiring flooring that could be installed efficiently while remaining durable enough for high daily foot traffic.</p>', '<p>Argil supplied click-lock SPC flooring with realistic oak wood finishes, allowing quick installation without compromising durability or design.</p>', '<p>The office received a modern, comfortable working environment with durable flooring that remains easy to clean and suitable for everyday commercial use.</p>', 'Oak Wood SPC Flooring', '2025-06-18', '1783421257_6Xc6HIAJ.png', '\"[\\\"1783421257_jJnrcjpD.png\\\",\\\"1783421257_FeWZuMVi.png\\\",\\\"1783421257_MBXV69VR.png\\\"]\"', 'Corporate Office SPC Flooring Project | Argil', 'See how Argil installed premium SPC flooring for a corporate office, delivering durability, fast installation, and elegant wood aesthetics.', 'spc flooring office,commercial spc flooring,office flooring project,oak spc flooring', 'published', 1, '2026-07-07 01:49:41', '2026-07-07 05:17:37'),
(14, 'Retail Showroom Interior with Premium SPC Flooring', 'retail-showroom-interior-with-premium-spc-flooring', 'Argil SPC flooring enhanced the visual appeal and durability of a premium retail showroom.', '<p>A fashion showroom required flooring that complemented contemporary interiors while supporting continuous customer traffic throughout the day. The design team selected Argil SPC flooring to create a warm, welcoming retail environment.</p>', 'Retail Interior Project', 'Retail', 'Mumbai, Maharashtra', 'SPC Flooring', 'Retail Showroom', '<p>Heavy customer movement required flooring that could maintain its appearance despite constant use.</p>', '<p>Argil supplied commercial-grade SPC flooring featuring authentic wood textures and wear-resistant construction.</p>', '<p>The completed showroom offers an inviting shopping experience with flooring that remains attractive and easy to maintain.</p>', 'Wood Finish SPC Flooring', '2025-02-08', '1783421166_AJn2fAs8.png', '\"[\\\"1783421166_lbRlQLxd.png\\\",\\\"1783421166_wsx7WaN1.png\\\",\\\"1783421167_2poLTeaa.png\\\"]\"', 'Retail Showroom SPC Flooring Project | Argil', 'Explore how Argil transformed a retail showroom using premium SPC flooring designed for durability and modern interiors.', 'retail showroom flooring,spc flooring showroom,commercial flooring project,wood finish spc', 'published', 1, '2026-07-07 02:12:15', '2026-07-07 05:16:07'),
(15, 'Hotel Vanity & Bathroom Quartz Installation', 'hotel-vanity-bathroom-quartz-installation', 'Premium engineered quartz surfaces created elegant and hygienic vanity areas for a boutique hospitality project.', '<p>&lt;p&gt;A boutique hotel sought premium vanity surfaces capable of withstanding continuous guest usage while maintaining a sophisticated appearance. &lt;b&gt;Argil engineered quartz&lt;/b&gt; provided an ideal combination of hygiene, durability, and modern aesthetics.&lt;/p&gt;</p>', 'Boutique Hospitality Project', 'Hospitality', 'Jaipur, Rajasthan', 'Quartz Surface', 'Bathroom Vanity', '<p>Hotel bathrooms require moisture-resistant surfaces that remain attractive despite frequent cleaning and continuous guest use.</p>', '<p>Argil supplied polished &lt;strong&gt; engineered quartz vanity tops &lt;/strong&gt;with consistent color, non-porous construction, and durable performance.</p>', '<p>The renovated bathrooms deliver a premium guest experience while simplifying routine housekeeping and maintenance.</p>', 'White Quartz Vanity Surface', '2025-04-24', '1783421974_U6zZxp0N.png', '\"[\\\"1783422048_Jm71BGrB.png\\\",\\\"1783422048_qqCybqb8.png\\\",\\\"1783422048_inv259aT.png\\\"]\"', 'Hotel Bathroom Quartz Installation Project | Argil', 'Discover how Argil engineered quartz enhanced hotel bathroom vanities with hygienic, durable, and elegant surfaces.', 'hotel quartz vanity,bathroom quartz project,engineered quartz hotel,hospitality quartz', 'published', 1, '2026-07-07 02:18:58', '2026-07-07 05:30:48'),
(16, 'Premium Residential Flooring Renovation with SPC', 'premium-residential-flooring-renovation-with-spc', 'Argil SPC flooring modernized a residential interior with stylish wood finishes and durable performance.', '<p>Argil SPC flooring modernized a residential interior with stylish wood finishes and durable performance.</p>', 'Residential Renovation Project', 'Residential', 'Surat, Gujarat', 'SPC Flooring', 'Living Room & Bedrooms', '<p>The renovation required flooring that could be installed efficiently while providing long-term durability and resistance to everyday household wear.</p>', '<p>Argil recommended premium SPC flooring with an authentic oak wood finish and click-lock installation system, minimizing disruption during renovation.</p>', '<p>The renovated home now features elegant, low-maintenance flooring that complements modern interiors while providing reliable daily performance for the family.</p>', 'Premium Oak SPC Flooring', '2025-09-15', '1783421752_zaKZpV5V.jpeg', '\"[\\\"1783421841_37jozLAb.jpeg\\\",\\\"1783421841_ildjMQRS.jpeg\\\",\\\"1783421841_TTb1GEoe.jpeg\\\",\\\"1783421841_6HTvsQFR.jpeg\\\",\\\"1783421841_iQcAtHGN.jpeg\\\"]\"', 'Residential SPC Flooring Renovation Project | Argil', 'Learn how Argil upgraded a residential apartment using premium SPC flooring with realistic wood aesthetics and long-lasting performance.', 'residential spc flooring,home flooring renovation,oak spc flooring,waterproof flooring project', 'published', 1, '2026-07-07 03:58:32', '2026-07-07 05:27:21');
